# GC23-11 bounded fleet classification (lane V23-F; PRD section 12 GC23-11, section 10
# "making every repository ALIVE" is a non-goal; ARD section 4; ARD section 26 F7).
#
# One sj:FleetClassification per repository of fleet/universe.json (21 repositories).
# Vocabulary: fleet/vocabulary.ttl (goal-graph-local; the semantic-jira-pack has no fleet
# classification terms). Checked by `python3 scripts/sjira/fleet_matrix.py
# check-classification` (exactly one row per universe repository; required iff
# CriticalPath; Successor rows name v23:GC-26.9.24; a repository a GC23 court script names
# must be CriticalPath). This graph declares scope only: it asserts no standing and no
# receipt. CriticalPath standing is derived by `check-standing` from admitted receipts at
# the exact head of each integration worktree.
#
# Every evidence row comes from fleet/observations.json (observed 2026-09-23T06:40:42Z:
# git fetch --all --tags --no-prune, rev-parse, symbolic-ref, rev-list --left-right,
# status --porcelain, gh pr list --state open) or from the file / run / PR it names.
#
# Required set: xaas and ggen_igniter (COORDINATION.md "Critical path = ggen_igniter + xaas").
# ash_a2a and autofde-lab are NOT required at this base: no GC23 court script executes
# either checkout (see their rows); the court-reference guard re-opens that question
# mechanically when a machinery lane's court names one of them.

# ── CriticalPath (required) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────

